Subject: [PATCH 8/8 RFC] ARM: dts: meson8b: attach the VDEC to its power domain

Meson8b has no canvas byte-order control, so the decoder still refuses to
stream, but the DT topology is the one the driver needs: the decoder takes
the AO bits from the pwrc domain instead of a sysctrl phandle, and the
existing canvas and clock references are unchanged.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/amlogic/meson8b.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/amlogic/meson8b.dtsi
index 4ded8eb..055b830 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/amlogic/meson8b.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/amlogic/meson8b.dtsi
@@ -27,8 +27,8 @@
 			clock-names = "dos_parser", "dos", "vdec_1";
 			resets = <&reset RESET_PARSER>;
 			reset-names = "esparser";
-			amlogic,ao-sysctrl = <&pmu>;
 			amlogic,canvas = <&canvas>;
+			power-domains = <&pwrc PWRC_MESON8_VDEC_ID>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 	};
